WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:09.880
[Drumming and music]

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:23.900
[Drumming]

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:26.540
[Narrator #1:] Any practice of medicine and research in the tropics

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:30.540
requires a new examination into the cause and nature of disease,

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.100
and in terms of treatment,

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.760
a different concept regarding the indigenous people

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:38.520
and the application of medicine to their specific needs.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:41.480
More often than not, the freshly-recruited medical worker

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.900
learns that he must reexamine the relations between people

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:50.820
and the relations to their environment that he had grown to accept as constants.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:55.140
The climate, in all its aspects, creates conditions often completely different

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:58.480
from those known to the uninitiated worker.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:02.880
The important issue of malnutrition and its direct and indirect relationships

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:07.670
to disease may lead him to an analysis of agricultural problems.

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:11.080
The way of life of the indigenous people may be so foreign to him,

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:15.540
that he must virtually become psychologist, anthropologist, and social worker.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:20.500
On the other hand, the prevalence of insert-borne parasitic diseases makes imperative

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:23.580
a knowledge of the basic biological sciences.

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:26.840
Thus, any study of tropical medicine must be prefaced

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:30.620
by an emphasis on both the ecological nature of the region

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.920
and the way of life of the people.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:34.000
In this instance,

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:41.120
we will examine the practice of medicine and medical research in the Republic of Liberia.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:44.500
Liberia lies in the Tropic Zone on the West Coast of Africa,

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:51.200
stretching from a point 280 miles north of the equator to a point 650 miles north.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.340
The land level rises from the coastline

00:01:53.340 --> 00:02:01.140
to 4000 feet in the mountain foothills some 150 miles inland.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:05.340
Liberia has been aptly characterized as a watershed area.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:09.480
The annual rainfall ranges from a maximum of 200 inches along the coast

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:12.600
to 70 inches up country.

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:16.700
The numerous rivers and their tributaries overflow during the rainy season,

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:20.300
when the temperature will fall to a low of 50 degrees.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:24.020
The annual mean maximum temperature is 86 degrees,

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:30.300
the mean minimum is 71 degrees, and the average annual humidity is 82 percent.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:33.560
In the dry season when the Harmattan Winds redden the sky

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:35.900
with the sands of the North African deserts,

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:39.100
the shade temperature rises to the high 90s.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:44.480
Under these conditions, mycotic infections of the skin are highly prevalent.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:48.540
Most of Liberia was originally covered by tropical rain forests.

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:53.600
Large areas have been cut over to meet the needs of a primitive agriculture.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:56.660
Yet the resultant sporadic cultivation has allowed

00:02:56.660 --> 00:03:01.280
second growth forests to repossess the land.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.400
The temperature range and high humidity are determinant factors

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:08.160
in the development of insect vectors of disease.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:15.600
On the other hand, the life economy of some insect species is such an intricate complex of physiological requirements,

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:22.620
that any slight environmental change can upset the delicate equilibrium on which survival depends.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:26.680
Such are the risks attending extreme specialization,

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:29.980
as is the case with the female tsetse fly.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:34.480
In the reproductive cycle, the most specific of conditions are required:

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.160
a permanent stream of water,

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:39.360
a sandy bank into which she inserts the larvae,

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.240
a fairly constant temperature,

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:46.460
and a low canopy of vegetation producing nearly 100 percent humidity.

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:53.300
In those areas of Liberia where the heavy jungle growth has been replaced by commercially-productive rubber trees

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.740
with their high branches and thin foliage,

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:58.800
the tsetse fly has disappeared.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:02.960
Many of the people's daily functions of survival constitute mechanisms

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:06.420
by which they are exposed to parasitic infection.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:11.480
A single body of water is often the village's source for fishing, bathing, and drinking.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:16.340
Thus, they come in contact with many of the insect and snail vectors.

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:25.520
[Music]

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:29.340
Life in Africa may appear to be lackadaisical to foreign eyes.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:35.440
Much infection seems due to an absence of precaution and a lack of interest in bettering their lives,

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:41.220
but the land and the climate are determinant factors conditioning concepts of hygiene.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:45.360
Life is far from easy, not to be plucked from the nearest tree.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:48.220
The currents keep the fish away from Liberia's coast,

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:53.500
and often a successful catch is made no closer than 80 miles off shore.

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:57.700
The torrential rainfall in the wet season leaches the soil.

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:02.000
The high soil temperature and the photoperiodic constancy,

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.360
12 hours night and 12 hours day,

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:09.000
curtail the growth of most grains and vegetables that come from cooler climates.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.240
When rice and casaba are to be planted,

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:14.260
the heavy forest must be cut down.

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:19.600
Without fertilization, each crop of rice exhausts the already weakened soil.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:21.740
As it must lie fallow for six years,

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:26.280
new jungle areas must be cleared.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:28.640
Then, at the end of the six year period,

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:31.160
the original plot is covered with scrub.

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:32.160
The cycle begins anew,

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:36.340
and the laborious cutting back of the jungle never ceases.

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:39.020
The dearth of protein is compounded by the unsuitability

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:41.700
of the soil to support forage crops,

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:47.820
and the presence of various livestock diseases, including trypanosomiasis.

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:51.640
With arrow or gun, the hunter finds little success,

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:54.500
or as small as the Liberian population is,

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:59.860
it has grown beyond the limit of its diminishing forests to support wild game.

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:02.840
With this limited diet, the shortage of protein,

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:05.720
and the mother's insufficient supply of milk,

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:09.900
the child's defense against infection is critically impaired.

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:14.980
Tools are primitive, and no matter how greatly we may admire the skill of the metal craftsman,

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:18.040
long and tedious hours of labor are required

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:22.040
to fashion the most simple implements and objects.

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:25.580
A division of labor is obvious and clearly defined,

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:29.820
but both sexes find the fruits of their labor minimal and uncertain.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.600
In such primitive societies,

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:36.640
superstition exists to conjure up answers to daily and seasonal mysteries.

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:40.680
In place of procedures born of an orderly appraisal of data,

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:45.360
the necessary understanding of nature is absent.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:48.140
Because there is no knowledge of the cause of disease,

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:51.820
the full disposal of sewage beyond the limits of water source contamination

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:53.680
is not practiced.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.800
Because rivers are everywhere accessible,

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:58.280
wells are seldom sunk.

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:01.260
In the unobjective terms of what is observable,

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:04.480
conclusions have been drawn that well water is stale.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:07.580
In a noble attempt to relate tropical cause and effect,

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:13.670
it is often believed that the degree of coldness of well water is the cause of colds.

00:07:13.690 --> 00:07:18.660
Thus, the existence of superstition is not due to an unwillingness to learn,

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:22.140
and a parting with ancient ways begins when the process

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:25.840
and the result become predictable.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:29.360
Until generations of individuals have learned from experience,

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:32.620
the mystical authority of the witch doctor will prevail.

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:36.860
Clay will continue to be used as both a cosmetic and a skin ointment.

00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:40.920
Disease will fester in isolation until it is sought out,

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:44.820
and no matter how friendly is the image of the friendly devil dancer,

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:50.220
he will for some time continue to represent the equation between primitive man's

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:57.380
lack of knowledge and nature's apparent caprice-like behavior.

00:07:57.380 --> 00:07:59.540
Against this background of primal need,

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:04.120
research and medical organizations and agencies are at work in Liberia,

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:06.680
scraping away the surface of myth,

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:13.440
building anew on the solid ground of need, an objective understanding of scientific process.

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:15.740
Emanating from the government of Liberia,

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:18.020
and led by its energetic president,

00:08:18.020 --> 00:08:20.240
the Honorable William V.S. Tubman,

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:25.720
there exists a program of ever-increasing medical facilities and public health projects.

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:30.160
The National Public Health Services under the direction of Dr. Jay N. Togba

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:32.800
provides and operates hospitals, dispensaries,

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:36.920
and conducts training programs for nurses, technicians, and sanitarians.

00:08:36.920 --> 00:08:38.640
As this trained force grows,

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:43.500
and the resultant education creates a new demand for modern medicine,

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:51.340
an increasing number of Liberian students will take up the study of medicine in the schools of Europe and America.

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:53.480
[Music]

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:56.490
The endeavor of the national Public Health Services is furthered

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:59.670
through cooperation with various international agencies.

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:02.300
In cooperation with the World Health Organization,

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:06.900
they have inaugurated a campaign to eliminate malaria and yaws

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:10.400
and with the United States International Cooperation Administration,

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:13.200
they are conducting a program of technical training,

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:16.440
in addition to an anti-malaria campaign.

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:22.200
Among the first medical efforts in Liberia were those of the various denominational missions.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:27.020
In the almost completely isolated villages, long before the penetration of roads,

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:30.020
they set up their hospitals and dispensaries,

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:36.720
and the personal histories of these medical pioneers constitute a saga of man's faith, ingenuity,

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:42.380
and unfaltering energy; a saga seldom equaled in the history of human dedication.

00:09:42.380 --> 00:09:45.980
[Music]

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:52.480
Operating on another level of motive are the two large commercial operations in Liberia.

00:09:52.490 --> 00:09:58.290
The Firestone Plantations Company has been growing and processing rubber since 1926.

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:04.820
[Music]

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:08.260
In recent years, the Liberia Mining Company has found success

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:10.960
in the extraction of high-grade iron ore.

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:15.280
These two companies employ close to 30,000 Liberians,

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:21.060
and provide them and their families with housing, community, and medical facilities.

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:24.220
Such medical programs extend beyond the direct results

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:27.960
of treating and immunizing the employees and their families.

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:29.980
Viewed only negatively,

00:10:29.990 --> 00:10:34.000
an epidemic among this labor force could cause havoc to the economy

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:35.460
of the country.

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:42.900
But, as the first step lies in the protection of the body of men,

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:49.650
an even more emphatic contribution is born in the mind of men.

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:54.020
They are operating the vehicles and machine tools of the industrial world.

00:10:54.020 --> 00:10:58.060
They are learning the agricultural science of plant breeding and grafting,

00:10:58.060 --> 00:11:01.940
and they are maintaining the chemistry of rubber processing.

00:11:01.940 --> 00:11:09.740
It is this skilled labor force that represents the population that is Liberia's future.

00:11:13.180 --> 00:11:16.970
Analyzed positively in the light of these occupational developments,

00:11:16.990 --> 00:11:22.210
the Liberians' increasing dependence on and knowledge of the world of medicine

00:11:22.210 --> 00:11:27.020
becomes an attendant factor in Liberia's social and economic growth.

00:11:27.020 --> 00:11:31.280
Serving as the fulcrum of health and sanitation of the Firestone Plantations,

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:34.260
two hospitals maintain over 200 beds,

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:37.100
staffed by 11 physicians and 75 nurses,

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:41.460
lab technicians, and orderlies.

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:44.860
Due to the high level of mechanization in the mining process

00:11:44.860 --> 00:11:47.300
and the consequently-limited labor force,

00:11:47.300 --> 00:11:49.520
the Bomi Hills Hospital is smaller,

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:55.500
but its facilities and services are equal to the best to be found in Africa.

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:59.700
Bomi is especially plagued with a heavily silted water supply,

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:02.840
and as a check on its modern filtration system,

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:07.520
a bacteria count is maintained at all major distributive points.

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:12.160
In both operations, prevention takes precedence over treatment.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:19.100
[Music]

00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:24.360
Sanitation and hygiene in the company villages constitute the basis of prevention,

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:32.040
but the education and vigilance of the villagers themselves is a prerequisite to that goal.

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:35.520
Under the guidance of directives developed by the medical staff,

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:39.380
each of the plantation villages possesses a trained sanitarian

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:43.620
who is periodically checked and upgraded through examinations.

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:49.360
The sanitarian maintains a continuity in the method and effectiveness of sewage disposal,

00:12:49.360 --> 00:12:53.660
and in general, is custodian to the health needs of his community.

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:58.820
The new pattern of symmetrically-designed villages takes hold with the residents.

00:12:58.820 --> 00:13:04.040
Seeing the benefits of drainages, planned and maintained thoroughfares, and recreation areas,

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:07.770
they also come to accept new and improved types of housing

00:13:07.770 --> 00:13:11.600
that radically depart from the traditional and inadequate hut.

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:19.080
[Music]

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:24.380
As the changing seasons bring changes in the density and species of insect vectors,

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:28.100
insecticide spraying teams move through the villages,

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:32.300
and even with new residents who have had little experience with medicine

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:36.940
and no knowledge of the relationship between insect vectors and disease,

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:42.720
the very elimination of the pests from the houses represents a newfound peace.

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:53.640
[Music]

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:57.400
Thus, the fullest performance of these medical programs is obtained

00:13:57.400 --> 00:14:01.680
by bringing prevention and treatment to the local working and living areas.

00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:08.060
In addition to maintaining nurses at the hiring centers, and clinics in the heavily-populated factory area,

00:14:08.060 --> 00:14:13.200
the plantation doctors conduct regular frequent clinics at 36 dispensaries,

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:17.980
strategically located across the 100,000 acres of the plantation.

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:20.760
[Music]

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:23.480
With such a program, illness is identified early.

00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:26.700
Guidance in the diet and care of the newborn is provided,

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:31.420
and the people learn that the practice of modern medicine is a methodical procedure,

00:14:31.420 --> 00:14:36.820
composed of objective knowledge, and requiring only their understanding and cooperation.

00:14:36.820 --> 00:14:41.700
They learn that the results of modern medicine tend to be orderly and stable,

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:50.080
and nonviolent and non-dramatic in contrast to the life or death prescription of the country medicine man.

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:54.980
Basic to all this activity, on both the public and private level, is research.

00:14:54.980 --> 00:15:02.480
In that singular interest, the Liberian Institute of the American Foundation for Tropical Medicine was, in 1946,

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:07.360
incorporated in the state of New York as a private nonprofit organization.

00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:11.740
In 1951, on a land grant from the government of Liberia,

00:15:11.740 --> 00:15:14.640
the present structures were completed with funds provided by

00:15:14.650 --> 00:15:18.780
Harvey S. Firestone, Jr. as a memorial to his father.

00:15:18.780 --> 00:15:23.680
Support of the institute comes from annual gifts made by American business corporations

00:15:23.680 --> 00:15:25.780
operating in the various tropical areas,

00:15:25.780 --> 00:15:27.380
including Liberia,

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:32.600
and by research grant funds provided by the United States Public Health Service.

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:40.280
The Institute's basic goal is to contribute to the more successful prevention and treatment of topical disease.

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:46.020
In such terms, it has successfully endeavored to fulfill a four-point program.

00:15:46.020 --> 00:16:03.620
[Music]

00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:06.180
Attracted to this opportunity from all over the world,

00:16:06.180 --> 00:16:09.520
scientists study the insect vectors and methods of control.

00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:13.660
While an outpatient clinic is maintained by the Institute,

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:21.440
the nearby plantation hospital sets aside beds for institute case studies requiring hospitalization.

00:16:21.440 --> 00:16:25.400
Numerous villages serve as laboratories of treatment and control,

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:29.920
and throughout Liberia, the Institute carries out collaborative projects

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:34.320
with such groups as American universities, the World Health Organization,

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:37.120
and the United States Public Health Service.

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:40.640
In view of the variety and density of tropical disease,

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:46.760
all of Liberia is available for medical study.

00:16:56.040 --> 00:17:01.600
[Narrator #2:] Neural leprosy has two manifestations, macula-anesthetic leprosy;

00:17:01.600 --> 00:17:09.900
a depigmentation of skin patches

00:17:09.910 --> 00:17:13.650
and mutilization with loss of digits.

00:17:20.360 --> 00:17:24.340
Nodular leprosy is often referred to as lion face.

00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:34.250
In Liberia, there are several leprosaria,

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:38.980
supported by the National Public Health Services and various missions.

00:17:38.980 --> 00:17:44.480
Here, at the Ganta Methodist Mission, under the direction of Dr. George W. Harley,

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:46.900
the discharge rate has been greatly accelerated,

00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:50.700
with the use of the new therapeutic agents.

00:17:50.700 --> 00:17:54.960
The incidence of leprosy in Liberia is not known.

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:57.480
Until more extensive studies are carried out,

00:17:57.480 --> 00:18:01.100
there can be no certainty of existing data.

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:05.440
While the few agencies in this field are contributing a valuable service,

00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:08.300
the impression must remain that no progress in control.

00:18:08.300 --> 00:18:12.940
[inaudible]

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:14.680
...made.

00:18:14.680 --> 00:18:19.900
However, the cooperative reaction of the patients, their obvious desire for the drugs,

00:18:19.900 --> 00:18:24.020
and the attendant growth of an interest in and understanding of disease,

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:28.600
reveals that given data and facilities, the disease can be eradicated.

00:18:57.140 --> 00:19:01.620
Yaws is widely prevalent among the Liberian population.

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:05.800
In the early stages, it is essentially a disease of the skin.

00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:14.380
Later, it becomes systemic, and the most troublesome late lesions are those of the bones, joints, and plantar surfaces of the feet.

00:19:14.380 --> 00:19:21.620
Goundou, an exostosis of the facial bones. It is considered by most authorities to be a tertiary lesion of YAWS.

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:35.840
Plantar or crab YAWS. This condition, which is characterized by the development of papillomata

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:38.040
under the thick skin of the sole, is very painful.

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:45.060
Eventually, the overlying skin breaks down, and ulcers form.

00:19:45.060 --> 00:19:50.300
Because it is highly contagious, the disease is one of the most difficult to eradicate, and the

00:19:50.300 --> 00:19:53.320
incapacitating degree of pain causes a heavy loss

00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:57.460
to the manpower of the country.

00:19:57.470 --> 00:20:02.630
Osteitis results in saber shins and deformities of the arms and fingers.

00:20:04.240 --> 00:20:07.800
Collaborative projects on the treatment of YAWS are being conducted by

00:20:07.800 --> 00:20:10.980
the National Public Health Services of Liberia,

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:13.020
the World Health Organization,

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:16.320
and the United Nations International Children's Emergency Fund.

00:20:26.020 --> 00:20:31.380
The filarial worm is transmitted by a species of fly of the genus Simulium,

00:20:31.380 --> 00:20:37.940
commonly called the black fly, which breeds in rapidly flowing streams.

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:40.920
Infection causes onchocercal dermatitis;

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:43.940
shown here with a superimposed pyogenic infection.

00:20:56.440 --> 00:21:02.020
And fibrous nodules. And in some instances, eye lesions.

00:21:06.100 --> 00:21:09.500
Here, a nodule in the pelvic region is being removed.

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:32.020
Onchocercosis is now considered by the World Health Organization

00:21:32.020 --> 00:21:34.900
to be the most urgent medical problems in Africa.

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:43.560
Bancroft's filariasis is due to a filarial worm parasite,

00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:46.900
Wuchereria Bancrofti, which invades the lymphatic system.

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:52.980
It is transmitted by a number of mosquito species very prevalent in Liberia.

00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:58.640
It is this parasite that gives rise to elephantiasis.

00:21:58.640 --> 00:22:03.640
Also, lymphangitis, adenitis, and other clinical conditions.

00:22:07.700 --> 00:22:11.160
Without the aid of a survey, which would be difficult,

00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:14.200
the prevalence of TB is not known.

00:22:14.200 --> 00:22:19.720
It is recognized as widespread in Liberia, as in most underdeveloped countries.

00:22:19.720 --> 00:22:23.660
Isolation hospitals are provided by the National Public Health Services,

00:22:23.660 --> 00:22:26.200
utilizing specific chemotherapy.

00:22:29.900 --> 00:22:32.280
The well-known tendency of the African

00:22:32.280 --> 00:22:35.440
to develop keloid growths is well exemplified here.

00:22:51.880 --> 00:22:54.840
Part of the growth was surgically removed,

00:22:54.850 --> 00:22:58.310
and it can be seen as recurring around the edges of the excision.

00:23:02.420 --> 00:23:06.900
Ainhum is a disease characterized by spontaneous amputation

00:23:06.900 --> 00:23:10.320
of the fifth and occasionally the fourth toe.

00:23:10.320 --> 00:23:16.340
It is brought about by constricting fibrous bands developing at the base of the toes.

00:23:16.340 --> 00:23:19.300
The disease is most prevalent in West Africa and Brazil.

00:23:19.300 --> 00:23:22.160
The cause is unknown.

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:31.480
Ulcerative processes of the skin, especially on the legs,

00:23:31.490 --> 00:23:35.330
are very common and in some instances, difficult to cure.

00:23:46.640 --> 00:23:53.760
African sleeping sickness is caused by the protozoan parasite trypanosoma gambiense,

00:23:53.760 --> 00:23:59.160
which is transmitted by the tsetse fly, Glossina palpalis.

00:23:59.160 --> 00:24:03.980
In its late stages, the disease is characterized by disorders of the central nervous system,

00:24:03.980 --> 00:24:08.440
usually resulting in lethargy and a stuporous condition.

00:24:08.440 --> 00:24:12.820
However, the hyper-reactivity shown by this patient can also occur.

00:24:29.560 --> 00:24:35.120
Smallpox has recurred in Liberia periodically in devastating epidemics.

00:24:35.120 --> 00:24:37.380
Although there has been some vaccination,

00:24:37.380 --> 00:24:40.980
the entire population is by no means protected.

00:24:40.990 --> 00:24:50.260
Until there is 100 percent vaccination, the threat of a recurrence exists.

00:24:50.260 --> 00:24:51.920
[Music]

00:24:51.920 --> 00:24:58.280
[Narrator#1:] The research work of the Liberian Institute of the American Foundation for Tropical Medicine extends beyond its 15 labs,

00:24:58.290 --> 00:25:02.800
lab animal houses, and workshops; all Liberia is its laboratory.

00:25:02.800 --> 00:25:08.540
Liberians eager to improve their country's strength take their own individual first step,

00:25:08.540 --> 00:25:10.720
and train as technicians.

00:25:10.720 --> 00:25:18.060
As the scientists possesses two methods of control where a carrier is involved: to destroy the transmitting vector,

00:25:18.060 --> 00:25:21.840
and to treat and prevent the effects of the parasite in the host,

00:25:21.840 --> 00:25:26.700
so too does he depend on the problem being attacked on more than one front.

00:25:26.700 --> 00:25:32.720
The basic conditions that weaken the body and cause susceptibility must also be eradicated.

00:25:32.720 --> 00:25:36.760
[Music]

00:25:36.760 --> 00:25:41.220
The Institute recognizes that one problem basic to treatment

00:25:41.220 --> 00:25:43.240
is the malnutrition of the people;

00:25:43.240 --> 00:25:45.320
a lack of protein in the diet.

00:25:46.300 --> 00:25:50.060
To help combat this scarcity, the Liberian Government,

00:25:50.060 --> 00:25:53.100
the United States International Cooperation Administration,

00:25:53.100 --> 00:25:56.820
and Firestone, are establishing fish ponds.

00:25:56.830 --> 00:26:30.130
[Music]

00:26:30.130 --> 00:26:35.800
The creation of such a supply of protein for each inland village is the final goal.

00:26:35.800 --> 00:26:38.260
[Music]

00:26:38.260 --> 00:26:41.940
With Liberia's climate ideally suited for tree crops,

00:26:41.940 --> 00:26:44.320
it is only natural that the work of the many rubber,

00:26:44.320 --> 00:26:47.980
coffee, and cocoa botanists is leaving a deep mark.

00:26:47.980 --> 00:26:51.240
Taking advantage of this profound cultural wedge,

00:26:51.240 --> 00:26:57.660
an ICA agronomist shows a tribal chief the increased resistance and productivity

00:26:57.660 --> 00:27:00.220
of a new variety of palm nut tree,

00:27:00.220 --> 00:27:03.120
the oil of which is an important food source.

00:27:03.120 --> 00:27:07.940
The move is on to educate a change from the growing of dry rice

00:27:07.940 --> 00:27:11.060
to the less toilsome and higher-yielding swamp rice,

00:27:11.060 --> 00:27:15.180
and the growing presence on the plantation and demonstration farms

00:27:15.180 --> 00:27:17.440
of mechanical tools, is producing an interest,

00:27:17.440 --> 00:27:19.940
which promises far-reaching results.

00:27:19.940 --> 00:27:37.200
[Music]

00:27:37.200 --> 00:27:40.720
On the medical side of health by drug and surgery,

00:27:40.720 --> 00:27:44.200
the stories of scientific treatment emanate from the plantation hospitals

00:27:44.200 --> 00:27:46.540
to display a folklore of magic;

00:27:46.540 --> 00:27:51.200
a tale spellbinding with its facets of sleep-producing aromas,

00:27:54.120 --> 00:27:55.720
painless incisions,

00:27:59.040 --> 00:28:00.340
and quick recovery.

00:28:00.340 --> 00:28:04.100
[Music]

00:28:04.100 --> 00:28:07.040
With such an enviable social position,

00:28:07.040 --> 00:28:10.920
the physician gains an opportunity to begin at the beginning,

00:28:10.920 --> 00:28:15.100
and the expectant mothers look forward to the scheduled prenatal clinics.

00:28:15.100 --> 00:28:19.520
[Music]

00:28:19.520 --> 00:28:21.940
But to the continued progress of this activity,

00:28:21.940 --> 00:28:24.170
research is always fundamental.

00:28:24.170 --> 00:28:26.840
In the malaria work of the Liberian Institute,

00:28:26.840 --> 00:28:30.460
a complete knowledge of the life habits of mosquito vectors

00:28:30.460 --> 00:28:32.080
and their relation to malaria,

00:28:32.080 --> 00:28:36.700
is an essential prerequisite to the establishment of a control program.

00:28:36.700 --> 00:28:40.820
In the laboratory, thousands upon thousands of mosquitoes are annually reared and used

00:28:40.820 --> 00:28:42.900
in a variety of studies,

00:28:42.900 --> 00:28:45.160
including experimental infections

00:28:45.160 --> 00:28:47.620
and the determination of the genetic factors

00:28:47.620 --> 00:28:51.080
in acquired tolerance to insecticides.

00:28:51.080 --> 00:28:56.040
To determine the fluctuations in specie population and density throughout the year,

00:28:56.040 --> 00:29:00.840
collecting trips are made daily to numerous localities over extended periods.

00:29:00.840 --> 00:29:02.800
To attract and capture the mosquitoes,

00:29:02.800 --> 00:29:05.800
teams of collectors set up portable hut traps,

00:29:05.810 --> 00:29:08.130
in which they spend rather fitful nights.

00:29:08.130 --> 00:29:33.330
[Music]

00:29:33.330 --> 00:29:36.950
By their growing understanding of the methodology of science,

00:29:36.950 --> 00:29:39.240
these technicians gain some added strength

00:29:39.240 --> 00:29:43.760
in resisting the normal desire to swat the little pests.

00:29:43.760 --> 00:29:48.120
[Music]

00:29:48.120 --> 00:29:53.260
Schistosomiasis or bilharzias is prevalent in large areas of Liberia.

00:29:53.260 --> 00:29:58.060
Institute surveys have shown close to 100 percent infection in some regions.

00:29:58.060 --> 00:30:02.900
The two species of schistosomes in Liberia, haematobium and mansoni,

00:30:02.900 --> 00:30:04.700
are carried by snails.

00:30:04.700 --> 00:30:08.800
Work is in progress to test methods of destroying the snail vectors,

00:30:08.800 --> 00:30:12.180
and to determine the effects of various drugs on the parasite.

00:30:12.180 --> 00:30:14.760
[Music]

00:30:14.760 --> 00:30:16.720
Across country at the mines,

00:30:16.720 --> 00:30:21.660
an institute staff member examines a group of children for enlargement of the spleen,

00:30:21.660 --> 00:30:26.580
to determine the effectiveness of a residual insecticide spraying program

00:30:26.580 --> 00:30:29.220
in the eradication of the insect carrier.

00:30:29.220 --> 00:30:34.740
Incidentally, umbilical hernias, such as this one, are very common among African children.

00:30:34.740 --> 00:30:38.720
However, a large proportion of the incidence disappears in adult life.

00:30:38.720 --> 00:30:59.660
[Music]

00:30:59.660 --> 00:31:04.500
Trypanosomiasis, sleeping sickness, is another disease prevalent in Liberia.

00:31:04.500 --> 00:31:07.060
The incidence, however, is not known. On a tour upcountry,

00:31:07.060 --> 00:31:11.000
the Institute's director, Dr. Max Miller,

00:31:11.010 --> 00:31:14.200
pays a visit to the clan chief of a group of villages

00:31:14.200 --> 00:31:20.040
to secure his cooperation and permission in locating cases of the disease.

00:31:20.040 --> 00:31:22.240
Old acquaintances exchange gossip,

00:31:22.240 --> 00:31:26.500
news of local crop conditions traded for a report on a local youngster,

00:31:26.500 --> 00:31:28.880
working as an institute technician.

00:31:28.880 --> 00:31:34.400
Then, with the ease of established trust, the chief leads the doctor to a nearby case,

00:31:34.400 --> 00:31:38.560
and the excited retinue, eager for a demonstration, follows.

00:31:38.560 --> 00:31:43.800
African sleeping disease is a disease of major importance to the health of Liberia.

00:31:43.800 --> 00:31:48.940
The Institute's work at the present time is mainly restricted to the testing of drugs

00:31:48.940 --> 00:31:52.200
and a limited surveying of the incidence of infection.

00:31:52.200 --> 00:31:54.460
As additional funds become available,

00:31:54.460 --> 00:31:57.800
research can be extended to a degree commensurate with the need.

00:31:58.840 --> 00:32:01.340
This case is an advanced one.

00:32:01.350 --> 00:32:04.870
The stage of infection is demonstrated by extreme lethargy.

00:32:04.870 --> 00:32:08.360
Walks only with the greatest difficulty and assistance.

00:32:08.360 --> 00:32:13.260
If left alone, he would show no interest in food, and die of starvation.

00:32:14.180 --> 00:32:17.280
The extreme emaciation obviously reveals

00:32:17.280 --> 00:32:20.500
that the case is rapidly progressing to the last stages.

00:32:20.500 --> 00:32:24.520
Because he is unable to perform the most elementary personal hygiene,

00:32:24.520 --> 00:32:28.820
he is covered with a skin infection, and is irritable when disturbed.

00:32:34.200 --> 00:32:37.420
An experiment in administering a malarial drug

00:32:37.420 --> 00:32:42.040
and the consequent blood surveys, moves into its ninth month.

00:32:42.050 --> 00:32:45.430
Two groups of villages serve the investigation.

00:32:45.430 --> 00:32:47.300
All the population of one-half the villages

00:32:47.300 --> 00:32:51.600
have been given monthly suppressive doses of anti-malarial drugs,

00:32:51.600 --> 00:32:56.000
while the population of the other half have taken placeboes, sugar pills.

00:32:56.000 --> 00:32:57.920
At the time of drug administration,

00:32:57.920 --> 00:33:03.840
a survey is made to determine the malaria parasite rate in the entire population group.

00:33:03.840 --> 00:33:06.780
In the light of the growing interdependence of nations,

00:33:06.780 --> 00:33:10.700
the necessary trading of energy for skills, skills for resources,

00:33:10.700 --> 00:33:14.620
and resources for a participation in all the wealth of man's achievement,

00:33:14.620 --> 00:33:17.600
there can be seen a kinship between the smallest,

00:33:17.600 --> 00:33:21.240
most unconscious endeavor, and the greatest need.

00:33:21.240 --> 00:33:26.660
Although the success of the survey is dependent on the village receiving the suppressives,

00:33:26.660 --> 00:33:29.820
it is no less indebted to the people taking placeboes.

00:33:29.820 --> 00:33:41.020
[Music]

00:33:41.020 --> 00:33:45.860
If the development of backward areas has become fundamental to the growing needs of all people,

00:33:45.860 --> 00:33:51.600
the eradication of tropical disease lies in the category of first things first.

00:33:51.600 --> 00:33:55.120
As evidence of the Liberian Institute's function, facility,

00:33:55.120 --> 00:33:56.980
and opportunity to this end,

00:33:56.980 --> 00:34:00.140
scientists from all over the world are drawn to it.

00:34:00.140 --> 00:34:04.880
They work in a country that is friendly to our concept of human dignity.

00:34:04.880 --> 00:34:10.320
For the Institute's very existence provides the example of American business abroad

00:34:10.320 --> 00:34:12.800
contributing to the health of man.

00:34:12.800 --> 00:34:16.800
By its ready acceptance of change when the benefits are clear,

00:34:16.800 --> 00:34:20.280
the population reveals its desire to progress,

00:34:20.280 --> 00:34:24.320
and the government, too, is anxious to make a dynamic contribution,

00:34:24.320 --> 00:34:27.320
because it recognizes that it cannot increase its voice

00:34:27.320 --> 00:34:30.260
among the nations by only clipping the coupons

00:34:30.270 --> 00:34:32.510
of the country's growing wealth.

00:34:32.510 --> 00:34:36.040
With this wealth of opportunity and cooperation,

00:34:36.040 --> 00:34:38.320
it is easy to see the pattern necessary

00:34:38.320 --> 00:34:40.380
in the development of the backward areas.

00:34:40.380 --> 00:34:47.740
[Music]

00:34:47.750 --> 00:34:51.750
There is a great prevalence of disease,

00:34:51.750 --> 00:34:56.010
an absence of proper foods,

00:34:56.010 --> 00:35:00.750
and a lack of knowledge concerning the realities of the world the people live in.

00:35:00.750 --> 00:35:06.160
[Music]

00:35:06.160 --> 00:35:07.920
Cure the disease.

00:35:07.920 --> 00:35:13.880
[Music]

00:35:13.880 --> 00:35:16.620
Free the people for productive enterprise,

00:35:16.620 --> 00:35:20.540
and the indigenous people will eagerly seek the knowledge necessary

00:35:20.540 --> 00:35:23.080
to further enrich their lives.

00:35:23.080 --> 00:35:26.380
[Music]

00:35:26.380 --> 00:35:32.160
The Liberian Institute's dedication to seek inexpensive methods of treatment and prevention

00:35:32.160 --> 00:35:34.320
attacks the core of the problem.

00:35:34.320 --> 00:35:39.460
To this end, the Institute should receive widespread support.

00:35:39.460 --> 00:35:41.720
With the new intercourse of trade,

00:35:41.720 --> 00:35:44.920
the dark continent's resources of soil and climate

00:35:44.920 --> 00:35:49.160
are only available as the health of the people is secure.

00:35:49.160 --> 00:35:54.100
In point of fact, the health of the world can benefit by so small,

00:35:54.100 --> 00:35:59.040
so unknowing a contribution as that being made by the Liberian people

00:35:59.040 --> 00:36:02.520
in both the test village and the control village.

00:36:02.520 --> 00:36:06.900
In one of the blood samples held against the African light,

00:36:06.900 --> 00:36:11.260
the image of all the world's well-being can be seen.

00:36:11.260 --> 00:36:13.060
[Music]

